Freshdesk Snapshot Analyzer - AI Prompt Log

## 0.0.1

### Prompt 1 - 2026-10-06

Create an application using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Jquery and any other requireds JavaScript Library for the following objecxtive with the following requirements
- The Application will read the excel files in a sepecific folder
- the excel files is a dump of Fresh desk
- the dump date can be oibtained from the files name, it is of the format FreshDesk_CRM_<dd-mm-yyyy>.xlsx, where <dd-mm-yyyy> mentions the dump date
- The application will analize the data from "Main Sheet" Sheet if ther are multiple sheets or the only sheet in the file.
- The analysis report will give the latest status of all the tickets reading the excel files, The Ticket Ids are unique
- There will be separate analysis report for each Group (from the Group Column)
- the Reports should have 
    - Ticket Id (from Ticket ID field)
	- Subject (from Subject field)
	- Created Date-Time (from Created time field)
	- ETA (from ETA field)
	- Resolved Date (from Date Part of Resolved time field)
	- Closed Date (from Date Part of Closed time field)
	- Assigned To (from Assignee field)
	- Raised By (from Full name field)
	- Email (from Contact ID field)
	- Age ( calculate based on Created Date, in days)
- Additionally Create 
   - a documentation.md file that records the complete application details, e.g. Objective, Workflow, use cases, user stories, changelogs with versioning in <major>.<minor>.<patch> format, starting with 0.0.1
   - a prompt.pmt file that records all the AI prompts made
   
### Implementation Notes

- Browser security does not allow a static page to silently scan an arbitrary folder. The application uses a user-approved directory picker where supported, with a multi-file selection fallback.
- Files are processed locally in the browser using SheetJS; jQuery is used for interface updates and interactions.
- Ticket age is measured against the newest valid dump date, making the result consistent with the selected historical snapshot rather than the computer's current date.

## 0.0.2

### Prompt 2 - 2026-10-06

Run a pass on the overall source code and fix/make changes/upgrade (as applicable) also update the documentation files (.md, .pmt)
- Add a Status Column in the reports that will state the latest status based on the different excel files
- Add a Sl. No. Column in the Report
- Make the default Folder to be "C:\Users\soumya.roy\OneDrive - SHYAM STEEL INDUSTRIES LIMITED\Projects\#Freshdesk"

### Implementation Notes

- Added Status from the latest ticket row and sequential Sl. No. values to both the on-screen report and CSV export.
- Added `server.js`, which binds to loopback only and reads the configured folder locally. Set `FRESHDESK_FOLDER` to override the default path.
- The app loads the default folder automatically when served by `node server.js`; manual browser folder and file selection remain available.
- Validated the status field and ETA cell values against exports in the configured folder; Excel-serial ETA dates are displayed as dates.

